Lotte?
We like you.

01:22:41.600 --> 01:22:44.800
We can see you're a kind
and decent woman...

01:22:44.880 --> 01:22:46.720
and so...

01:22:46.760 --> 01:22:50.640
we've decided to offer you
a place in John Malkovich with us...

01:22:50.720 --> 01:22:52.560
if you like.

01:22:57.280 --> 01:22:59.520
Dr. Lester...

01:22:59.560 --> 01:23:01.880
you've been so kind to me...

01:23:01.960 --> 01:23:03.800
and trusting.

01:23:03.880 --> 01:23:05.920
And...

01:23:06.000 --> 01:23:10.280
there's just something I think you
should know about the Malkovich vessel.

01:23:10.360 --> 01:23:12.440
[ Woman On Speaker ] John's here
to see you. Should I send him in?

01:23:12.560 --> 01:23:16.360
Of course send him right in. Don't ever
keep him waiting again, you understand?

01:23:16.440 --> 01:23:18.720
- [ Angry Muttering ]
- [Door Opens]

01:23:18.760 --> 01:23:21.480
[ Clears Throat ]
Hey, John.

01:23:21.560 --> 01:23:24.680
Great to see you.
Sorry about the cunt at reception.

01:23:28.680 --> 01:23:32.640
Sorry about the cunt at reception.
Please, have a seat.

01:23:35.560 --> 01:23:39.480
Can I get you anything?
Coffee? Water?

01:23:39.560 --> 01:23:41.520
No, thank you.

01:23:41.560 --> 01:23:43.840
- Teresa, get me chicken soup.
- Okay.

01:23:43.920 --> 01:23:47.080
Chicken soup?
Chicken soup?

01:23:51.760 --> 01:23:55.560
Larry? Uh...
I want to get right to the point.

01:23:55.680 --> 01:23:59.400
From now on, I'm no longer an actor.
I'm a puppeteer.

01:23:59.480 --> 01:24:01.800
Okay. Great.

01:24:06.440 --> 01:24:09.520
And I would like
to redirect my career...

01:24:09.600 --> 01:24:12.440
so that from now on
the name John Malkovich...

01:24:12.520 --> 01:24:15.680
will be synonymous with puppets.

01:24:15.720 --> 01:24:18.520
Sure. Sure.
No problemo.

01:24:18.600 --> 01:24:22.360
Poof, you're a puppeteer.
Just let me make a couple calls.

01:24:33.960 --> 01:24:36.320
[Laughing Continues]

01:24:44.360 --> 01:24:48.080
Honey? Maxine?

01:24:48.160 --> 01:24:50.280
Maxine?

01:24:50.360 --> 01:24:52.200
I'm busy.

01:24:54.320 --> 01:24:57.880
Maxine, honey, it's on!

01:24:57.920 --> 01:25:01.720
[ Dramatic ]

01:25:04.600 --> 01:25:07.040
Yeah, there's the truth,
and there are lies...

01:25:07.080 --> 01:25:10.400
and, uh, art always tells the truth,
even when it's lying.

01:25:10.480 --> 01:25:13.040
[Male Narrator]
The enigmatic John Malkovich...

01:25:13.080 --> 01:25:16.280
one of the world's greatest entertainers
and the man who reinvented. ..

01:25:16.360 --> 01:25:18.200
how we view puppeteering.

01:25:18.280 --> 01:25:20.720
Tonight we look at the man
above the strings...

01:25:20.800 --> 01:25:22.880
and the woman behind the man.

01:25:22.960 --> 01:25:27.680
Raised in Evanston, Illinois,
Malkovich had a lifelong interest
in theater arts...

01:25:27.800 --> 01:25:30.160
and as a young man was
one of the founding members...

01:25:30.240 --> 01:25:34.200
of Chicago's world-renowned
Steppenwolf Theatre Company.

01:25:34.280 --> 01:25:37.320
From there, it was a simple hop, skip
and jump to Broadway accolades...

01:25:37.400 --> 01:25:39.240
and Hollywood stardom.

01:25:39.320 --> 01:25:43.360
But nothing could prepare the public
for what was to come next.

01:25:43.440 --> 01:25:46.040
And so it was that just
eight short months ago...

01:25:46.120 --> 01:25:49.200
John Malkovich dropped the bombshell
that sent shock waves...

01:25:49.240 --> 01:25:52.000
through the entertainment community.

01:25:52.080 --> 01:25:55.400
Turning his back on his
former profession,
Malkovich had to start from scratch...

01:25:55.480 --> 01:25:58.920
and pay his dues allover again
as a fledgling puppeteer.

01:25:59.000 --> 01:26:02.120
[ Clears Throat ] Hello, ladies
and gentlemen, I'm John Malkovich.

01:26:02.200 --> 01:26:04.960
It's-- It's the-- I miss--

01:26:05.000 --> 01:26:07.360
I'm really John Malkovich.
[ Giggling ]

01:26:07.440 --> 01:26:09.760
[Narrator]
From these inauspicious beginnings...

01:26:09.840 --> 01:26:13.520
John Malkovich's rise
to stardom was fast and furious.

01:26:13.560 --> 01:26:17.000
His breakout performance occurred
at this year's Emmy Awards--

01:26:17.040 --> 01:26:19.280
- [Narration Continues]
- It's really good!
I look really amazing.

01:26:19.360 --> 01:26:21.200
I'd fuck me.

01:26:21.280 --> 01:26:23.400
If there's anything
that upsets me about it...

01:26:23.480 --> 01:26:26.080
it's feeling like
if move into it too quickly...

01:26:26.160 --> 01:26:28.640
I'll be, you know, deemed an imitator.

01:26:28.720 --> 01:26:31.560
But, um, I think that once
we all get the courage...

01:26:31.600 --> 01:26:34.520
to just follow through on
our instincts, like Malkovich has...

01:26:34.600 --> 01:26:37.240
I think that, uh, a lot of us
will move into puppetry.

01:26:37.280 --> 01:26:41.320
[Narrator]Malkovich's rise to fame
brought about a renaissance
in puppeteering.

01:26:41.400 --> 01:26:44.160
No, no, no. What are you doing?
What are you doing?

01:26:44.200 --> 01:26:47.960
- I'm making him weep, John.
- You're making him weep,
but you are not weeping.

01:26:48.000 --> 01:26:50.160
Don't ever-- [ Beep ]
with your audience.

01:26:50.200 --> 01:26:53.160
Until the-- the puppet becomes...

01:26:53.200 --> 01:26:56.480
an extension of you, it's a novelty act.

01:26:56.560 --> 01:26:58.480
It's, uh--
It's Topo Gigio.

01:26:58.600 --> 01:27:00.080
No?

01:27:02.520 --> 01:27:05.200
[Man]
He's a technical genius.

01:27:05.280 --> 01:27:07.440
He breathes life
into inanimate objects.

01:27:07.520 --> 01:27:10.080
It's a very godlike thing...

01:27:10.160 --> 01:27:14.080
to be able to take something and,
you know, make it live.

01:27:14.120 --> 01:27:16.360
[Narrator]
He was the talk of the town...

01:27:16.440 --> 01:27:19.440
from the Beltway to Broadway...

01:27:19.480 --> 01:27:23.080
aided in no small part by
his new wife and manager, Maxine Lund.

01:27:23.160 --> 01:27:26.640
In Maxine,
Malkovich had found his mentor...

01:27:26.680 --> 01:27:29.200
his muse, his inspiration.

01:27:29.320 --> 01:27:33.440
In Malkovich,
Maxine had found the love of her life.

01:27:33.440 --> 01:27:37.760
- [ Panting ]
- There, there, my dear. Relax.

01:27:37.840 --> 01:27:41.120
This travesty will
all be over with by morning.

01:27:41.200 --> 01:27:43.840
And the crowds have been
absolutely sensational...

01:27:43.920 --> 01:27:47.240
and, um, I'd just like to thank God
for giving us this opportunity...

01:27:47.320 --> 01:27:49.160
to share our creative vision.

01:27:49.240 --> 01:27:52.680
[Narrator]Nothing was impossible
for John and Maxine in the early days.

01:27:52.760 --> 01:27:56.200
Their union was a joyous one,
and together they worked tirelessly...

01:27:56.280 --> 01:27:58.640
to further Malkovich's
puppeteering career.

01:27:58.680 --> 01:28:00.840
John Malkovich, the artist...

01:28:00.920 --> 01:28:03.280
and Maxine, the entrepreneur--

01:28:03.400 --> 01:28:05.360
they make this character...

01:28:05.480 --> 01:28:08.840
this protean figure
that we cal John Malkovich.

01:28:08.920 --> 01:28:12.600
[Narrator]But some say Maxine
has changed since becoming pregnant...

01:28:12.680 --> 01:28:14.920
recoiling from the limelight...

01:28:15.000 --> 01:28:17.640
and, rumor has it,
from her husband's affections.

01:28:26.320 --> 01:28:28.920
[ Whispering ]
I'm so sorry.

01:28:33.720 --> 01:28:36.560
[Bing]Malkovich shows us...

01:28:36.600 --> 01:28:40.200
a reflection of ourselves,
our frailties...

01:28:40.280 --> 01:28:45.520
and our, you know,
desperate humanity.

01:28:45.600 --> 01:28:50.160
That's what makes him one of
the most relevant artists of our time.

01:28:50.240 --> 01:28:53.800
[Narrator]And what does the future
hold for John Horatio Malkovich?

01:28:53.880 --> 01:28:58.280
Well, to quote the Bard,
"He's got the world on a string. "

01:28:58.360 --> 01:29:03.120
As the poet said, "The puppeteer's voice
need not merely be the record of man.

01:29:03.200 --> 01:29:05.600
It can be one of the pillars,
the props...

01:29:05.680 --> 01:29:09.040
to help him endure and prevail,"
and I believe that.

01:29:10.120 --> 01:29:11.960
It's over!

01:29:13.800 --> 01:29:15.720
Max?

01:29:15.760 --> 01:29:18.440
I've gotta head down to A.B.T. now.

01:29:18.520 --> 01:29:21.640
I've got the "Swan Lake"
benefit tonight, okay?

01:29:21.720 --> 01:29:24.280
But when I come back,
we can maybe celebrate...

01:29:24.320 --> 01:29:27.880
Malkovich's big four-four.

01:29:27.960 --> 01:29:30.520
Okay? Jesus!

01:29:30.600 --> 01:29:33.440
Why couldn't I have found
the portal to a younger body?

01:29:33.520 --> 01:29:37.200
What if l--
What if I fall tonight and break my hip?

01:29:43.840 --> 01:29:46.600
[Classical]

01:29:52.000 --> 01:29:54.000
[Continues]

01:30:25.520 --> 01:30:28.360
Like that, little girl?

01:30:28.440 --> 01:30:30.280
Huh, lamb?

01:30:32.560 --> 01:30:34.400
I love you.

01:30:54.560 --> 01:30:56.800
